From 6d635bd5d070f5297c7361f35fe997899da1327e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 01:19:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda/hip: the attention Q projection co-launched inside the
 K/V grouped mmvq (+0.6% decode)

Round 37 found the last independent matvec pair in the graph and could not
merge it: after 0049 pinned the attention block order to Q, K, V the three
projections are adjacent and share one activation, but the grouped mmvq
kernel is single-type and 0021 leaves attn_q at Q6_K while attn_k/attn_v
stay Q8_0.

This is 0047 machinery applied to a grouped host: mul_mat_vec_q_grouped
gains a second-vec_dot-type guest that is a WHOLE standalone
mul_mat_vec_q<type_g,1,false,false>. gw is the warp count the guest own
launch gives one row (4 for Q6_K/ncols=2048 after the trim), so
blockDim.y/gw = 2 guest rows share a host block, blocks_per_iter_g stays
derived from the guest FULL compile-time nwarps, and the cross-warp
exchange keeps the trimmed warps +0.0f slots. Bit-identical by
construction, same as 0045-0048.

Block order follows the 0045 rule, and it inverts here: the guest is the
LARGE launch (8192 rows, 24.6us) and the host the small one (1024 rows,
6.9us), so the guest goes at the TAIL. Merged grid is 5120 blocks x 8
warps = exactly the 32768 + 8192 warps the two separate launches had.

541 -> 531 dispatches/token (-10, all matvec); the pair costs 28.8us
instead of 24.6 + 6.9 = 31.5us.

vs a binary built from the parent commit (f741ad9ad), LD_LIBRARY_PATH +
ldd verified, arms alternated: tg128 162.68 -> 163.67 (+0.61%, 4/4
separated), pp512 4910.8 -> 4910.0 (flat). Decode-path perplexity
3.9382 on both arms over three loads each; server greedy 6/6
byte-identical at the decode shape including a 1000-token prompt.

GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_XTYPE_GUEST=0 restores the two separate launches.
